title: 'App-server codex sessions: deliver the global cross-repo inbox via the ingress loop (B137 follow-up)'
updated_at: "2026-07-12T03:02:27Z"
---
B137 made the codex frontend hook identity-only (drains nothing) for app-server sessions, to close a nested-codex cross-repo mail theft (env markers propagate to descendants; the hook can't distinguish the attached frontend from a nested codex). Consequence: an app-server session's GLOBAL (cross-repo/sessions-broker) inbox is not delivered by the hook. Not a regression (pre-B137 the hook delivered under the wrong thread-id identity, so it never delivered the app-server global inbox either), but a functional gap. Fix: have the C2c_codex_ingress delivery loop (which owns arrival-time delivery for the attached app-server session and CAN distinguish the real attached thread) also surface the session's global/cross-repo inbox, without reopening the nested-theft vector. Ref: B137 report + local findings .collab/findings/2026-07-12T17-04-21Z-b137-codex-appserver-dual-identity.md (gitignored).